# Round 18, C1-12 (follows), the tie: two rows of x[a] in one version, each with a span (2027.. and 2027-06..): step 3
# leaves them tied, refused (L §5.3, §4.6 step 4, LOAD-OVERLAP).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
input x[k in ks]: money PLN
def r[k in ks, d in days]: money PLN = x[k] at d
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  x[a] = 5
  x[a] = 7 governs 2027..
  x[a] = 8 governs 2027-06..
  x[b] = 1
ask q: r[a, 2026-06-01], r[a, 2027-06-01], r[b, 2027-06-01]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-OVERLAP rows m.tally:16 and m.tally:17 of x overlap at [a] in one version (m.tally:17)
